Historical evidence recorded before the skeleton migration. Counts, pending statuses, temporary handles and next-step instructions describe that checkpoint; consult the current development Record before acting.

The first computing block is installed: seven new lessons connect digital representations, contracts, loop invariants/termination, operation/storage counts, execution, an original stock-tracing program and review. Five shared lessons (`rc-files`, `rc-values`, `rc-functions`, `rc-io`, `rc-schema`) retain their original identities, imports, prose and routes. The thirteen-Record progression starts at `@computing-core` and ends at `@computing-foundation-review`. Existing Sundnes and Python source identities are reused; no duplicate source Record or downloaded media was added.

The worked `stock_trace.py` checks every event before accepting its candidate state. It returns the accepted prefix and first invalid event, distinguishes invalid types from invalid initial bounds, rejects Boolean counts, and preserves its immutable input. The receipt-before-issue example exposes a capacity violation hidden by the final total. The alternative day ordering demonstrates that event-level and whole-day acceptance are different contracts. A loop invariant and a separate termination argument complement finite tests; neither the program nor those tests claim that real inventory assumptions are true.

The extracted original program passed 58,590 exhaustive finite-grid cases against independently recomputed prefix sums. Boundary cases, fourteen malformed-input cases, a large exact integer, input preservation, binary/text examples, operation-count identities and fresh-process repeatability brought the check count to 175,906. Executions with different working directories, hash seeds and time zones gave identical output. The actual interpreter was Python 3.14.8. Selected official 3.14 type, control-flow and exception documentation was inspected; its web pages identify patch 3.14.10, which is recorded separately from the executed runtime. Sundnes publisher metadata and contents were checked; whole assigned chapters/exercises were not fully audited.

Post-install checks passed: warnings-as-errors `cargo check --locked -p lince-resources --features publication --tests`; exact 69-Record core selection and directed reachability; all 44 authored broad/core/source discovery entrances reaching the same 1,545-document composition; 29,126 local references; 2,879 unique explicit Hephaestus identities; and preservation of all sixteen original subject compositions. The five reused programming lessons are unchanged after removing only their added core continuation. Reproducible computation still loads independently as 212 documents. The corpus parser passed for 2,881 files and 2,919 Records, and the planning register passed with 262 Records and all 134 pending subjects.

The combined core integration test is updated and compiles, but has not yet run for the current 69-Record composition. It checks all six root branches and every expected core edge, selected membership/reachability, source exclusion, four standalone shared formations, contextual/external references, fresh reopening after relocation and preservation of the stock program. Runtime discovery uses three structurally distinct entries (a source, an intermediate lesson and the new terminal review); static discovery checks every authored entrance. Repeated runtime traversal from each equivalent area map was removed to keep validation proportionate as discovery grows. The physics snapshot test still exercises its earlier, larger runtime entry sample; let it finish and collect the result.

The two live runs remain `88787` (original nineteen-test regression) and `38804` (42-Record physics snapshot). Both have been revalidated as active and consuming CPU, with no failures reported so far. Their results do not substitute for the updated combined test. Finish the current engineering/inquiry breadth pass, update its exact expected membership, then run the relevant combined core test without launching another duplicate full regression. Keep the tested composition stable during that run or use an explicitly identified immutable snapshot. Investigate actual failures; do not treat a quiet live process as stopped.

